      "side": 1,
      "message": "There won\u0027t be binary data because `content_str \u003d content.decode(\u0027latin-1\u0027, errors\u003d\u0027replace\u0027)` converts that to text (and then re-encodes it to utf-8 here if it\u0027s present). In other words, if there\u0027s binary data left after `mutool -a` and after stripping the header, it\u0027ll get corrupted. (\"best-effort\" etc.)\n\nI think outside of streams but inside of objects (which is all we keep), PDFs shouldn\u0027t contain binary data (?)",
